@startuml agent-authoring-current-and-fix
' ============================================================================
'  agentd AGENT AUTHORING - the write-scope deadlock (2026-08) and the
'  ONE-AUTHORITY fix. STATUS: BUILT (uncommitted) - pinned by
'  tests/unit/test_agent_authoring_paths.py (registry.agent_roots +
'  registry.create_from + AgentService._agent_roots + tool delegation).
'  Activity-flowchart view, same conventions as web-agent-request-flow.puml,
'  agent-publish-and-ownership-flow.puml, tenant-isolation-current-and-fix.puml.
'
'  THE DEADLOCK, one sentence:
'    create_agent writes where the REGISTRY says the caller's agents live
'    (the per-account overlay - correct), but check_write judges it against a
'    scope expanded from WHERE THE AGENT-BUILDER'S OWN FILES SIT (the shared
'    catalogue - stale) - so the compliant write is refused and the refusal
'    message steers the model toward the non-compliant one.
'
'  WHY THE FIX IS NOT A PATCH ON THE TOOL: the platform already has ONE
'  doctrine, proven three times over - a per-caller fact is resolved ONCE at
'  a choke point by the subsystem that OWNS it, carried as a VALUE, and no
'  consumer ever re-derives it:
'
'    egress      owner IN identities        ownership.may_observe (isolation fix)
'    models      whose key pays this turn   model_proxy.turn_key + accounts ctxvar
'    sandbox     what may this tool do      CapabilityResolver from tool metadata
'
'  Authoring is the LAST subsystem still deriving "where does the caller's
'  world live" by itself (from static file layout). The fix is to finish the
'  doctrine, not to special-case the tool: the REGISTRY is the single
'  authority for agent placement, and everything that needs the answer -
'  scope expansion, creation, collision, ownership stamping - ASKS it.
'
'  Render (from this folder):
'    java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng agent-authoring-current-and-fix.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #6A6A6A
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4E5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam partitionBorderColor #9AA0B5
skinparam partitionFontStyle bold
skinparam partitionFontSize 13

title Agent authoring - the write-scope deadlock + the one-authority fix\nthe REGISTRY owns "where do this caller's agents live"; scope, creation, collision and\nownership all ASK it - no consumer re-derives, no mode branches, every agent inherits it instantly

start

partition "0 . THE DOCTRINE - already proven 3x   (same daemon, all modes)" #E8F0FE {
  :**per-caller facts are resolved ONCE, at a choke point,
  by the subsystem that owns them, and consumed as VALUES**;
  :**egress** - who may see this frame or file: ownership.may_observe
  over identities pinned per connection (the tenant-isolation fix);
  :**models** - whose credential pays this turn: model_proxy.turn_key
  reads the accounts contextvar - BYOK direct, cloud via our proxy,
  hosted metered per account - tools never branch, never hold keys;
  :**sandbox** - what an untrusted plugin may do: CapabilityResolver
  derives grants from the tool's own metadata (needs_model, paths),
  the broker clamps and meters - the plugin code never knows;
  :authoring is the LAST subsystem outside the doctrine -
  it derives "where does the caller's world live" BY ITSELF;
}

partition "1 . THE DEADLOCK (TODAY) - two answers to one question" #FDECEA {
  :user signs in (desktop cloud or web) - the connection
  carries an ACCOUNT, so the registry's overlay resolver
  activates: reg.agents_dir now answers
  `.agentd/accounts/<acct>/agents`
  (per-caller, dynamic - CORRECT, the identity plan working);
  :the agent-builder's scope token `<agents_dir>` was expanded
  by AgentService._expand_paths as **agent_dir.parent** - the
  parent of wherever the BUILDER'S OWN definition sits, i.e.
  the shared catalogue `v2/agents`
  (static, layer-blind, account-blind - STALE);
  if (create_agent writes to the overlay?) then (yes - the compliant path)
    :check_write judges the overlay path against the
    stale scope -> **WriteRefused** - the path the
    RULES require is the path the SCOPE forbids;
  else (model falls back to `write`)
    :the refusal text ("write under that agent's own
    directory") steers the model into authoring
    DIRECTLY under the shared `v2/agents` - which the
    stale scope PERMITS;
    :=> bypasses the overlay AND ownership stamping -
    on hosted, a record-less SHARED agent that
    default-privacy then hides from its own creator;
  endif
  :=> the builder agent burns its whole budget
  reconciling two systems that genuinely disagree -
  "stuck", but not confused: both readings were true;
}

partition "2 . TWO SIDE-GAPS, SAME ROOT - a second creation path" #FDECEA {
  :registry.create() is the path that follows ALL the rules:
  places via _write_target, collides against _current()
  (everything the caller can SEE, so an overlay skeleton
  can never shadow a curated id), stamps `.agentd-meta.json`
  at birth via ownership_store.stamp_create;
  :create_agent re-implements that half itself: writes files
  directly + reg.add() - so it **never stamps ownership**
  (add only reads records) and its collision check is
  **d.is_dir() on one layer only** (would shadow a curated
  agent from the overlay);
  :root cause is structural: TWO creation paths, one of which
  re-derives placement, collision and ownership instead of
  asking the subsystem that owns them;
}

partition "3 . THE FIX - ONE AUTHORITY, ASKED, NEVER RE-DERIVED" #E6F4EA {
  :**the rule**: "where do THIS caller's agents live" has ONE
  owner - the registry (_write_target / _current / roots).
  Every consumer asks; none derives from file layout;
  :**a) scope follows the caller** - _expand_paths stops
  reading agent_dir.parent and asks the registry:
  `<agents_dir>` expands to BOTH roots - the shared
  catalogue AND the caller's overlay when the connection
  has one. Expansion already runs at RunContext creation,
  inside the connection's context, so the per-account
  answer is right automatically. _protected_paths gets
  the same treatment;
  :**b) creation becomes ONE path** - split by ownership
  of the knowledge: the TOOL keeps the CONTENT half
  (skeleton TOML grammar, key order, identity/heartbeat,
  refusal wording - the model-facing craft), the REGISTRY
  keeps the WORLD half (placement, layer-aware collision,
  stamp-at-birth, live add). create_agent DELEGATES -
  both side-gaps die structurally, not by patching checks
  into the tool;
  :**c) nothing else moves** - models, sandbox and egress
  already consume caller context at their own choke
  points; authoring simply joins the same doctrine.
  No agent.toml changes anywhere: every agent that says
  `<agents_dir>` gets a caller-shaped scope with zero
  edits, today's agents and every future one alike;
}

partition "4 . WHAT EACH MODE FEELS   (same code, different values)" #E0F2F1 {
  :**local BYOK (signed out)** - no account, no overlay:
  registry answers the shared catalogue alone; scope,
  placement and collision all agree exactly as today,
  new agents stamped owner "local". Byte-for-byte;
  :**desktop cloud (signed in, daemon on the user's PC)** -
  account -> overlay: new agents land in the ACCOUNT layer,
  stamped to the account, publishable under that identity,
  scope covers shared + overlay, so previously-authored
  shared agents stay editable (installed ones stay guarded
  by the protected set);
  :**hosted web** - account always present -> every created
  agent is born in the creator's own layer, stamped, private
  by default, visible and editable only through ownership
  rules the rest of the platform already enforces; the
  operator (machine token, no account) writes the shared
  layer - the deployment's own, a value not a branch;
}

partition "5 . WHY EVERY AGENT OBEYS INSTANTLY   (choke points)" #E8F0FE {
  :the fix lives in TWO process-level seams - AgentService
  (scope expansion at RunContext creation) and the registry
  (the one creation path) - no per-agent code, no per-tool
  code, no client code;
  :any tool that writes files passes check_write, and
  check_write reads the RunContext - so every authoring
  tool (write, create_tool, scaffold_ui, create_agent)
  inherits caller-shaped scope from the same seam;
  :ownership stamped at birth on the ONE creation path means
  publish, `mine`, edit-permission and hosted visibility all
  read a RECORD everywhere - the presumption fallback goes
  back to being legacy-only, as designed;
}

stop

note right
  ==== REUSED, NOT INVENTED ====
  _write_target / _current / agents_dir,
  ownership_store.stamp_create, the accounts
  contextvar and the RunContext carrier all
  exist and are tested. The fix rewires who
  ASKS whom - it adds no new concept, which
  is why it lands in all three modes at once.

  ==== KNOWN RESIDUE, later ====
  * refusal wording in check_write should name
    the overlay explicitly once scope is fixed
  * protected set (installed agents) should
    cover overlay installs, same derivation
  * registry.create()'s skeleton is poorer than
    the tool's (no version) - the merged path
    keeps the tool's richer content half
end note

legend left
  | Piece | Today | After the fix |
  | `<agents_dir>` scope token | agent_dir.parent - static, layer-blind | registry-answered: shared + caller overlay |
  | create_agent placement | reg.agents_dir (overlay) - then REFUSED | same target, scope agrees - accepted |
  | creation paths | two (registry.create vs tool DIY) | one - tool authors content, registry places |
  | ownership record | stamped only on registry.create path | stamped at birth on every creation |
  | collision check | tool: one layer; registry: all visible | one layer-aware check in the registry |
  | models / billing | already doctrine-compliant (funnel) | unchanged |
  | sandbox grants | already doctrine-compliant (resolver) | unchanged |
  | local BYOK | works (single layer) | identical - overlay absent, values degenerate |
  | desktop cloud | DEADLOCKED on create | creates into account layer, stamped |
  | hosted web | deadlock OR unstamped shared agent | born private, stamped, publishable |
endlegend

@enduml
